Future Funding Requirements

We expect our expenses to increase substantially in connection with our ongoing activities, in particular as we continue to advance LB-102 and any of our future product candidates through clinical trials, as well as additional costs associated with operating as a public company.

As of December 31, 2025, we had cash, cash equivalents and marketable securities of $295.2 million, which does not include net proceeds from our $100 million private placement in February 2026. Based on our current plans, we believe that our existing cash, cash equivalents and marketable securities, including net proceeds from our private placement in February 2026, will be sufficient to meet our anticipated operating and capital expenditure requirements into the second quarter of 2029.

